Z||000004||rogergarrison||07-11-2001||09:12 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by fierobaby:<BR><B>We put some sort of in and the CO count went up! so I believe my father put in an oxygen sensor in...hes going to take it to work and warm up the car alot before he takes it tomorrow...by chance would any of you know if perhaps you can get collector plates in Ohio for this car oh and it had 87156 Miles on it I think or about there</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE>]<P>You can get Ohio collector plates for anything as long as you have another car registered in your name. Dont you have a relative in a nearby city/county where you can register it. Cincy and Cleve are the only ones that chk emmissions. I know mine wouldnt pass a test - I dont even have an O2 sensor.<P>Just had this quick thought. If you have collectors or Historical tags, Im pretty sure emmissions isnt required. chk DMV<P><p>[This message has been edited by rogergarrison (edited 07-11-2001).]||||reg||1
